                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Fee reporting</strong></td>
                    <td>Income &amp; Expenditure and a payment history</td>
                    <td>Thirteen reports from the day book to the income statement, with CSV on every list — Chapter 12</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Statements</strong></td>
                    <td>Printed from the browser</td>
                    <td>An issued A4 PDF with a verification footer, for the bursar and for the parent</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Term close</strong></td>
                    <td>The proprietor asked for the numbers</td>
                    <td>The term summary PDF is emailed automatically at term end; a weekly outstanding-fees email runs during the term</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Debtors</strong></td>
                    <td>One row per child</td>
                    <td>One row per family, expandable to each child, with a phone number and a drafted reminder</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Results</strong></td>
                    <td>Entry only</td>
                    <td>A four-stage approval chain, HOD and year-group reports, term remarks, and a report card with a verification code — Chapters 10 and 14</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Privacy</strong></td>
                    <td>Some parent screens checked only that you were signed in</td>
                    <td>Every parent screen checks the relationship — invoices and statements included</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Mobile</strong></td>
                    <td>Usable on a laptop</td>
                    <td>Built for a 360-pixel phone first: no sideways scrolling, every action thumb-sized, every field large enough that the page does not zoom</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="note">
        <strong>Upgrade note for 1.0 schools.</strong> Old invoices that were created as "tuition" by the bulk importer are converted to the academic ledger so they appear in the new reports. If a figure in a 1.0 report does not match a 2.0 report, the 2.0 figure is the correct one: it is calculated from invoices and confirmed payments only.
    </div>

    <p>Questions the manual does not answer should be raised with the school's EDUS support contact rather than worked around — a shortcut in one term becomes a disputed figure at the next.</p>
</div>

<script>
    document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
        const menuToggle = document.getElementById('menuToggle');
        const sidebar = document.getElementById('sidebar');
        const overlay = document.getElementById('sidebarOverlay');
        const sidebarLinks = sidebar.querySelectorAll('a');

        // Function to toggle the menu open/closed
        function toggleMenu() {
            sidebar.classList.toggle('open');
            overlay.classList.toggle('active');
        }

        // Open/Close menu when the hamburger button is clicked
        menuToggle.addEventListener('click', toggleMenu);

        // Close menu when the dark overlay is clicked
        overlay.addEventListener('click', toggleMenu);

        // Close menu when a link inside the sidebar is clicked
        sidebarLinks.forEach(link => {
            link.addEventListener('click', () => {
                // Only close it automatically if we are on a mobile screen
                if (window.innerWidth <= 768) {
                    toggleMenu();
                }
            });
        });
    });
</script>
</body>
</html>